What is RAG?
RAG stands for Retrieval-Augmented Generation. It is a technique that combines two core ideas:

🔍 Retrieval — Searching and fetching the most relevant data from a knowledge base before answering
✍️ Generation — Using a Large Language Model (LLM) to craft an accurate, context-aware answer from the retrieved data
In simple terms: before answering a question, the model first searches for relevant information, then uses it to generate a better, more accurate response.
Analogy
Think of RAG like an open-book exam. Instead of answering purely from memory, the student (LLM) is allowed to look up the textbook (knowledge base) before writing the answer — resulting in a far more accurate response.
